# Instruction fidelity (always-on)

- **Talk:** plain English; answer first; say each point **once** — no rephrasing the same idea. Length as needed (3 lines or 20); table only when nothing else is clearer; brief summary last. Detail → `VISION/CURSOR_PROMPT_01.md` § Human communication.
- **Scope:** user ask only. Extra work (tests, docs, refactors) → say what/why, wait for approval. Rules → same file § Scope & fidelity.
- **Plan / review / comment / suggest** → words only, no edits, until they say **go**. If the plan looks wrong, say so briefly.
- **Commit / push** = commit **and push to GitHub** unless local only; report hash + push output.
- **Doubt** → one short question, then wait.

# No approval = no edit

Do not change the repo — code, CSS, config, tests, docs, rules, typos — unless they **explicitly approved that exact change**.

**Not approval:** silence, a question, frustration, past tasks, “go” on A while you also change B.

**Is approval:** “Go — [exact scope].” / “Fix X only.” / “Yes, items 1 and 3.”

**Before any edit:** say what files and behaviour you will change → **wait for go** → implement only that → verify → report.

If you edited without approval → say so at once; offer revert; do not add more unapproved fixes.

# Claims vs code

Shipped behaviour must match docs and UI. If not tested or not true → list in `PROJECTS/SmartBeads/GPT_PROJECT_STATUS_01P.md` § Integrity (human may remove). Never half-wire a feature while status says it works. Evidence rules → `VISION/AGENT_RULE_05P.md` § Evidence-Based Claims.
